<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Hardware Configuration</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments were conducted on a single NVIDIA H100 80GB GPU. The total computational budget of $196 was allocated as follows:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Synthetic data generation: $42</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Supervised fine-tuning experiments: $98</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reinforcement learning optimization: $56</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Hyperparameter Configuration</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Supervised Fine-Tuning</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">Learning Rate: 1e-4
Batch Size: 16
Gradient Accumulation Steps: 1
Epochs: 5
Warmup Ratio: 0.08
Weight Decay: 0.01
LoRA Rank: 16
LoRA Alpha: 32
LoRA Dropout: 0.05
Target Modules: ["q_proj", "k_proj", "v_proj", "o_proj",
                 "up_proj", "down_proj", "gate_proj"]
Mixed Precision: bfloat16
Gradient Checkpointing: Enabled
Max Sequence Length: 2048
</pre>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Reinforcement Learning (GRPO)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><pre id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">Learning Rate: 5e-5
Per-Device Batch Size: 16
Gradient Accumulation Steps: 4
Max Steps: 248
Temperature: 0.7
Top-p: 0.95
Beta (KL penalty): 0.05
Number of Generations per Prompt: 8
Max New Tokens: 532
Reward Scaling: "batch"
GAE Lambda: 0.95
Clip Range: 0.2
</pre>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Data Processing Pipeline</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The synthetic data generation pipeline processes documents through the following stages:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Document Chunking</span>: Split documents into 2000-character segments with 200-character overlap</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sequential Extraction</span>: Process chunks sequentially, maintaining memory across chunks</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Augmentation</span>: Generate multi-field combinations with token count constraints (532-1900 tokens)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Validation</span>: Ensure JSON validity and schema compliance for all training examples</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stratification</span>: Balance training data across document types and extraction complexity levels</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reward function implementation uses the following similarity thresholds:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">String similarity (embedding-based): Cosine similarity with MiniLM-L6-v2</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Numerical similarity: Relative difference with 1.0 penalty for &gt;100% deviation</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Date similarity: Temporal distance with exponential decay (half-life = 365 days)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">List similarity: Bipartite matching with threshold <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.35</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Boolean similarity: Exact match (1.0 for match, 0.0 for mismatch)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Training Data Examples</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following examples illustrate the diversity of extraction tasks in our synthetic training dataset:</p>
</div>
